Z||000001||88-DOHC||12-02-2001||02:56 AM||||You talking about the molding?  <P>Anyway, bondo is a bad choice anyway. It doesn't like moisture and it doesn't stiffen the underlying structure enough to keep it from flexing thus cracking it. There is fiberglass version of bondo that might work. Although its mostly used for areas that are prone to water. Your best bet would probably be fiber glass.||||reg||1
